{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>When the Most High gave nations as inheritance.</b> That he gave each and every nation its inheritance." "<b>When he separated the children of man.</b> In the generation of the dispersion, when he separated them and each man went to his place." "<b>He established the boundaries of peoples according to the number of the children of Israel.</b> He designated an inheritance for the twelve tribes, who had not yet been born, and delivered it to the twelve sons of Canaan — for they are the servants of the sons of Shem, as it is written: ״ויהי כנען עבד למו״ — so that he could not contest it at all, for whatever a servant acquires, his master acquires. And they guarded it until Israel, their masters, came and took it from their hand. And so he explained above, at the end of the portion of Kedoshim. And the sons of Canaan were twelve, as it is written: ״וכנען ילד את צידון בכורו ואת חת ואת היבוסי ואת האמורי ואת הגרגשי ואת החוי ואת הערקי ואת הסיני ואת הארודי ואת הצמרי ואת החמתי״ — and they are eleven, and afterward ״נפוצו משפחות הכנעני״, for one of his families split into two, and from it emerged the Perizzite, who is not listed here — behold, twelve, corresponding to the number of the children of Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:02.560790876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}